# --- Cloudflare Pages routing ---
#
# 1) Missing hashed assets MUST return a real 404 — never fall through to the
#    SPA index.html fallback. The `/assets/*` rule in `_headers` stamps
#    `Cache-Control: immutable, max-age=1y` by URL, so a fallback served for a
#    not-yet-propagated asset hash gets cached at the CF edge as
#    `200 text/html immutable` and is then served to EVERY client until a manual
#    "Purge Everything". That is what breaks the CSS on deploy ("Refused to apply
#    style ... MIME type text/html"). A 404 status is not cached/applied the same
#    way, so the edge self-heals once the real asset lands.
/assets/*  /404.html  404

# 2) SPA fallback for real navigation routes (real static files are served first,
#    before these rules, so this only catches client-side routes like /calendar).
/*  /index.html  200
